Mode-2 M5 capture instrumentation — apply to the HOST open driver
/root/open-gpu-kernel-modules before running scripts/mode2_capture_host.sh.

Target: src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/fifo/kernel_fifo.c, function
kfifoGetHostDeviceInfoTable_KERNEL, immediately AFTER the
pRmApi->Control(... NV2080_CTRL_CMD_FIFO_GET_DEVICE_INFO_TABLE ...) call
returns NV_OK (around line 2066, before the numEntries>MAX check). Dumps the
real per-page table so Mode-2's fake GSP can replay it.

Insert:

        // --- NVKVM_CAP capture (remove after capture) ---
        {
            NvU32 _i, _j;
            NV_PRINTF(LEVEL_ERROR, "NVKVM_CAP DEVINFO base=%u num=%u bMore=%u\n",
                      pParams->baseIndex, pParams->numEntries, pParams->bMore);
            for (_i = 0; _i < pParams->numEntries; _i++)
            {
                NV2080_CTRL_FIFO_DEVICE_ENTRY *_e = &pParams->entries[_i];
                for (_j = 0; _j < 16; _j += 4)
                    NV_PRINTF(LEVEL_ERROR,
                        "NVKVM_CAP e%u d%u %08x %08x %08x %08x\n",
                        _i, _j, _e->engineData[_j], _e->engineData[_j+1],
                        _e->engineData[_j+2], _e->engineData[_j+3]);
                NV_PRINTF(LEVEL_ERROR,
                    "NVKVM_CAP e%u pbdma %u,%u fault %u,%u np %u name %s\n",
                    _i, _e->pbdmaIds[0], _e->pbdmaIds[1],
                    _e->pbdmaFaultIds[0], _e->pbdmaFaultIds[1],
                    _e->numPbdmas, _e->engineName);
            }
        }
        // --- end NVKVM_CAP ---

NOTE: A broader capture (every ROUTE_TO_PHYSICAL control) would instead hook
rpcRmApiControl_GSP in src/nvidia/src/kernel/vgpu/rpc.c right after
_issueRpcAndWait returns, dumping {cmd, rpc_params->status, paramsSize, and the
first paramsSize bytes of rpc_params->params}. Start with the device-info-table
(the current blocker); add the rpc.c hook if later controls also need real data.

The engineData[] indices (ENGINE_INFO_TYPE_*) are defined in
src/nvidia/inc/kernel/gpu/fifo/kernel_fifo.h: ENG_DESC, RM_ENGINE_TYPE, RUNLIST,
RUNLIST_PRI_BASE, MMU_FAULT_ID, IS_HOST_DRIVEN_ENGINE, etc. — useful when baking
the replay table into nvkvm_m3_service_cmdq (key on cmd 0x20801112, return the
captured page for the requested baseIndex; flat copy, NOT FINN).
